 R←Test_Live_01(stopFlag batchFlag);⎕IO;⎕ML;⎕TRAP;filename;cfg;cp;mp;connection;rc;msg;log
⍝ Optional: sends a real email through a real SMTP server.
⍝ Runs only when the environment variable SMTP_TEST_CONFIG holds the name of a JSON5 file like this:
⍝ ```
⍝ {Server: "smtp.example.com", Port: 465, Secure: 1, Userid: "me@example.com", Password: "…", To: "me@example.com"}
⍝ ```
⍝ `From` is optional and defaults to `Userid`. Keep that file outside the repository: it holds a password.
⍝ In batch mode the test checks the return code only; otherwise it asks whether the email arrived.
 ⎕IO←1 ⋄ ⎕ML←1
 ⎕TRAP←(999 'C' '. ⍝ Deliberate error')(0 'N')
 R←T._NotApplicable
 filename←2 ⎕NQ'.' 'GetEnvironment' 'SMTP_TEST_CONFIG'
 :If 0=≢filename
     :Return
 :EndIf
 R←T._Failed

 cfg←⎕JSON⍠('Dialect' 'JSON5')⊢⊃⎕NGET filename
 cp←⎕NEW SMTP.ConnectionParameters
 cp.Server←cfg.Server
 cp.Port←cfg.Port
 cp.Secure←cfg.Secure
 cp.Userid←cfg.Userid
 cp.Password←cfg.Password
 mp←⎕NEW SMTP.MailParameters
 mp.To←cfg.To
 :If 0<cfg.⎕NC'From'
     mp.From←cfg.From
 :EndIf
 mp.Subject←'Live test from SMTP''s ',(⊃⎕SI),': Jäger, Łódź, {⍵/⍨2=+⌿0=⍵∘.|⍵}'
 mp.Body←'Line one' '.' '.leading dot' 'APL: Prim←{⍵/⍨2=+⌿0=⍵∘.|⍵}'
 mp.AddAttachment'./Test-Files/CrashReport.html'
 connection←⎕NEW SMTP.Connection(,⊂cp)
 (rc msg log)←connection.Send mp
 →T.PassesIf 0=rc
 :If ~batchFlag
     →T.PassesIf 1 CommTools.YesOrNo'Did ',cfg.To,' receive an email with APL characters in subject and body, the lines "." and ".leading dot", and an HTML attachment?'
 :EndIf

 R←T._OK
⍝Done
